IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-interpretation`
IMPORT `g6-art15-16-deregistration`
IMPORT `g6-art17-after-deregistration`
IMPORT `ind-b-tests-fixtures-g6`

-- ind-b-tests-art15-17: independent tests of Articles 15 to 17 (group G6), by test author ind-b.
-- Every expected value comes from work/ind-b/expectations.md, written from the Law before this module's imports were opened; each assertion cites its row id.
-- A section headed "reading checks" tests a non-default reading of a fork against what that reading itself says.

§ `Article 15 -- deregistration on application (rows E15-01 to E15-07)`

-- E15-01: complied, no ground relating to the proposals: the Commissioner MUST deregister; deregistering discharges it; refusing does not.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` `ind-b6 A` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` `ind-b6 A` TRUE TRUE FALSE) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`deregister the entity` `the Commissioner`) 1))
-- E15-03: refusing on a ground not relating to the proposals does not discharge the duty to deregister.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` `ind-b6 A` TRUE TRUE FALSE) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`refuse to deregister the entity on grounds relating to the proposals` `the Commissioner`) 1))
-- E15-02: complied, a ground relating to the proposals: refusing discharges, and so does deregistering.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` `ind-b6 A` TRUE TRUE TRUE) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`refuse to deregister the entity on grounds relating to the proposals` `the Commissioner`) 1))
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` `ind-b6 A` TRUE TRUE TRUE) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`deregister the entity` `the Commissioner`) 1))
-- E15-04: nothing requested: no 15(2) duty, and the entity has complied.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 15(2) the entity must provide the information requested` TRUE FALSE)
-- E15-05: an entity that is not a registered charity cannot apply; a registered charity may.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 15(1) the registered charity may apply to be deregistered` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 15(1) the registered charity may apply to be deregistered` TRUE)
-- E15-06: the applying entity must provide what the Commissioner requested about its proposals; providing it discharges the duty.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 15(2) the entity must provide the information requested` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 15(2) the entity must provide the information requested` TRUE TRUE) 0 (LIST EVENT `a registered charity` (`provide the Commissioner with the information or document requested` `a registered charity`) 1))
-- E15-07 and A-03 (reading A as to the duty): not complied with 15(2): no duty to deregister arises.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` `ind-b6 A` TRUE FALSE FALSE)

§ `Article 16 -- deregistration in other cases (rows E16-01 to E16-13)`

-- E16-01: no longer meets the charity test, proper notice that has run its time, proportionate: MAY deregister.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 the Commissioner may deregister` FALSE EMPTY (`ind-b6 grounds` FALSE FALSE TRUE) (JUST `ind-b6 a proper notice`) `ind-b6 day`
-- E16-02: misled into registering (unintentionally, by a third person): MAY.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 the Commissioner may deregister` TRUE EMPTY (`ind-b6 grounds` TRUE FALSE TRUE) (JUST `ind-b6 a proper notice`) `ind-b6 day`
-- E16-03: failed to comply with a required steps notice: MAY.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 the Commissioner may deregister` TRUE (LIST `ind-b6 an unmet notice`) (`ind-b6 grounds` FALSE FALSE TRUE) (JUST `ind-b6 a proper notice`) `ind-b6 day`
-- E16-04: a prescribed circumstance: MAY.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 the Commissioner may deregister` TRUE EMPTY (`ind-b6 grounds` FALSE TRUE TRUE) (JUST `ind-b6 a proper notice`) `ind-b6 day`
-- E16-05: no prior notice: may not.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 the Commissioner may deregister` FALSE EMPTY (`ind-b6 grounds` FALSE FALSE TRUE) NOTHING `ind-b6 day`
-- E16-06: the prior notice gave no reasons: may not.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 the Commissioner may deregister` FALSE EMPTY (`ind-b6 grounds` FALSE FALSE TRUE) (JUST (`ind-b6 notice` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)) `ind-b6 day`
-- E16-07: the prior notice did not invite objections within a specified time: may not.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 the Commissioner may deregister` FALSE EMPTY (`ind-b6 grounds` FALSE FALSE TRUE) (JUST (`ind-b6 notice` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE)) `ind-b6 day`
-- E16-08: not satisfied it is proportionate: may not.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 the Commissioner may deregister` FALSE EMPTY (`ind-b6 grounds` FALSE FALSE FALSE) (JUST `ind-b6 a proper notice`) `ind-b6 day`
-- E16-09: no ground: may not.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 the Commissioner may deregister` TRUE EMPTY (`ind-b6 grounds` FALSE FALSE TRUE) (JUST `ind-b6 a proper notice`) `ind-b6 day`
-- E16-01 as a trace: the Commissioner's written notice exercises the power.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 16(1) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` `ind-b6 A` TRUE FALSE EMPTY (`ind-b6 grounds` FALSE FALSE TRUE) (JUST `ind-b6 a proper notice`) `ind-b6 day`) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`deregister the entity by written notice` `the Commissioner`) 1))
-- E16-11: satisfied the entity no longer exists: MUST deregister, with no prior notice or proportionality.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 16(2) the Commissioner must deregister the entity that no longer exists` `ind-b6 A` TRUE TRUE NOTHING `ind-b6 day`)
-- E16-12: not so satisfied: no 16(2) duty.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 16(2) the Commissioner must deregister the entity that no longer exists` `ind-b6 A` TRUE FALSE NOTHING `ind-b6 day`)
-- E16-13 and A-04 (reading A): before the objection period specified has run out, the Commissioner may not deregister.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 the Commissioner may deregister` FALSE EMPTY (`ind-b6 grounds` FALSE FALSE TRUE) (JUST `ind-b6 a proper notice`) (YMD 2026 2 5)
-- E16-03: a notice whose time has not yet run out is not yet failed (F6.19 A), on 2026-01-20.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` `ind-b6 A` (LIST `ind-b6 an unmet notice`) (YMD 2026 1 20)
#ASSERT `Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` `ind-b6 A` (LIST `ind-b6 an unmet notice`) (YMD 2026 2 2)
-- Decision and basis records (IP27, IP32), as the Law names them.
#ASSERT `Art 16 the basis of deregistration` `by written notice under Article 16(2) because the entity no longer exists` EQUALS `the entity no longer exists`
#ASSERT `Art 16 the basis of deregistration` `on the entity's own application under Article 15(3)(a)` EQUALS `on the entity's own application under Article 15`

§ `Article 17(1) -- retention and the registered number (rows E17-01 to E17-07)`

-- E17-01 to E17-03 (convention X, taken): deregistered on 2020-03-15; the last day of retention is 2030-03-15; the information may be discarded from 2030-03-16.
#ASSERT `Art 17(1)(a) the last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 deregistered on 15 March 2020` EQUALS YMD 2030 3 15
#ASSERT `Art 17(1)(a) the Commissioner may discard the information on` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 deregistered on 15 March 2020` EQUALS YMD 2030 3 16
-- E17-05, E17-06 (X with clamp, taken): deregistered on 2020-02-29: the last day is 2030-02-28.
#ASSERT `Art 17(1)(a) the last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 deregistered on 29 February 2020` EQUALS YMD 2030 2 28
-- E17-01 as a rule: discarding within the ten years does not discharge the prohibition (that it is a breach and not a standing rule is shown by the positive control at the end of this file).
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 17(1)(a) the Commissioner must retain the information for 10 years` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 deregistered on 15 March 2020`) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`discard the information registered in respect of the entity` `the Commissioner`) 100))
-- E17-07: the number may not be given to another charity, ever (2075).
#ASSERT `Art 17(1)(b) the registered number may not be assigned on the day` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 deregistered on 15 March 2020` (YMD 2075 1 1)

§ `Article 17(2) to (4) -- retrospective effect (rows E17-08 to E17-19)`

-- E17-08: all four conditions, under Article 16: retrospective from 2020-01-01, for all purposes (E17-19: the date deregistered is the past date).
#ASSERT `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 retrospective to 1 January 2020`
#ASSERT `Art 17(3) the date from which the termination takes effect` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 retrospective to 1 January 2020` EQUALS JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)
#ASSERT `Art 17(3) the date deregistered` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 retrospective to 1 January 2020` EQUALS YMD 2020 1 1
-- E17-09: on application under Article 15: not retrospective; deregistered on the day of the decision.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 deregistration` `on the entity's own application under Article 15(3)(a)` (YMD 2020 3 15) NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 17(3) the date deregistered` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 deregistration` `on the entity's own application under Article 15(3)(a)` (YMD 2020 3 15) NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) TRUE) EQUALS YMD 2020 3 15
-- E17-10: the past date not specified in the notice: not retrospective.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 deregistration` `ind-b6 misled` (YMD 2020 3 15) (JUST (YMD 2020 2 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) NOTHING TRUE)
-- E17-11: not determined to be retrospective: not retrospective.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 deregistration` `ind-b6 misled` (YMD 2020 3 15) (JUST (YMD 2020 2 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) FALSE)
-- E17-12: not satisfied the grounds existed since a past date: not retrospective.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 deregistration` `ind-b6 misled` (YMD 2020 3 15) (JUST (YMD 2020 2 1)) NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) TRUE)
-- E17-13: under 16(2) (no longer exists), with (b) to (d): retrospective.
#ASSERT `Art 17(2) the deregistration takes effect retrospectively` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 deregistration` `by written notice under Article 16(2) because the entity no longer exists` (YMD 2020 3 15) NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) TRUE)
-- E17-14: an act of 2020-03-01, before the notice of 2020-07-01: not rendered an offence.
#ASSERT `Art 17(4) the act is not rendered an offence by the retrospective effect` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 retrospective, notice of 1 July 2020` (YMD 2020 3 1)
-- E17-15: an act of 2020-08-01: not protected.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 17(4) the act is not rendered an offence by the retrospective effect` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 retrospective, notice of 1 July 2020` (YMD 2020 8 1)
-- E17-16: an act of 2019-12-31 (before the past date): no offence.
#ASSERT `Art 17(4) the act is not rendered an offence by the retrospective effect` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 retrospective, notice of 1 July 2020` (YMD 2019 12 31)
-- E17-17 and A-06 (reading A, taken): an act on the day of the notice is not "before the date": not protected.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 17(4) the act is not rendered an offence by the retrospective effect` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 retrospective, notice of 1 July 2020` (YMD 2020 7 1)
-- E17-18 and A-05 (reading A, taken): an act of 2020-06-15, after the reasons notice and before the deregistration notice: protected.
#ASSERT `Art 17(4) the act is not rendered an offence by the retrospective effect` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 retrospective, notice of 1 July 2020` (YMD 2020 6 15)

§ `Article 17(5) to (11) -- the remaining property (rows E17-20 to E17-34)`

-- E17-20: property acquired before deregistration remains: (6) to (11) apply.
#ASSERT `Art 17(5) paragraphs (6) to (11) apply` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 deregistered on application` (LIST (`ind-b6 property` (YMD 2019 6 1) TRUE))
-- E17-21: only property acquired after deregistration: they do not.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 17(5) paragraphs (6) to (11) apply` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 deregistered on application` (LIST (`ind-b6 property` (YMD 2020 6 1) TRUE))
-- E17-22: the remaining property all spent: they cease to apply.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 17(5) paragraphs (6) to (11) apply` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 deregistered on application` (LIST (`ind-b6 property` (YMD 2019 6 1) FALSE))
-- E17-20: the entity must apply the remaining property for the preserved purposes.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 17(6) the entity must apply the remaining property for the preserved purposes` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Art 17(6) the preserved charitable purposes` `ind-b6 a registered company charity` EQUALS LIST "the advancement of education"
-- E17-23: no power to amend the preserved purposes, whatever the constitution says.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 17(7) the entity has power to amend the preserved purposes or statement` TRUE TRUE
-- E17-24: the entity may apply to the court; the court may make an amending order.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 17(8) the entity may apply to the court to amend the preserved purposes or statement` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 17(8) the court may make an amending order and any ancillary order` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- E17-25: the AG applies; conduct that would have been misconduct: the court may use its Article 14 powers.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 17(9) the court may exercise its Article 14 powers over the deregistered entity` TRUE `the Attorney General` TRUE FALSE `an order appointing a person to be a governor`)
-- E17-26: a governor who first notified the AG of the intention and the reasons may apply; the court may then act.
#ASSERT `Art 17(10) the governor may apply under paragraph (9)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 17(9) the court may exercise its Article 14 powers over the deregistered entity` TRUE `a governor` TRUE FALSE `an order appointing a person to be a governor`)
-- E17-27, E17-28: a governor who did not first give the AG notice of the intention AND the reasons may not apply.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 17(10) the governor may apply under paragraph (9)` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 17(10) a governor may not apply without first notifying the Attorney General` FALSE)
-- E17-29: an application by the Commissioner: no 17(9) power.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 17(9) the court may exercise its Article 14 powers over the deregistered entity` TRUE `the Commissioner` TRUE TRUE `an order appointing a person to be a governor`)
-- E17-30: no remaining property: no 17(9) power.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 17(9) the court may exercise its Article 14 powers over the deregistered entity` FALSE `the Attorney General` TRUE TRUE `an order appointing a person to be a governor`)
-- E17-31: neither (a) nor (b): no power.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 17(9) the court may exercise its Article 14 powers over the deregistered entity` TRUE `the Attorney General` FALSE FALSE `an order appointing a person to be a governor`)
-- E17-32: the AG applies; necessary to protect the remaining property: MAY.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 17(9) the court may exercise its Article 14 powers over the deregistered entity` TRUE `the Attorney General` FALSE TRUE `an order restricting transactions or payments without the court's consent`)
-- E17-33: the AG may take over a governor's application, and then withdraw it (or proceed).
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 17(11) the Attorney General may take over the application of a governor` TRUE)
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 17(11) the Attorney General may take over the application of a governor` TRUE) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Attorney General` (`take over the application of a governor` `the Attorney General`) 1, EVENT `the Attorney General` (`withdraw the application` `the Attorney General`) 2))
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 17(11) the Attorney General may take over the application of a governor` FALSE)

§ `Reading checks for Articles 15 to 17 (expected values from each reading's own words)`

-- F6.1 B (the Commissioner may refuse) and C (must refuse) where 15(2) was not complied with; D: the Law states no rule (a refusal).
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` (`the readings taken but with F6.1 read as` `the Commissioner may refuse to deregister`) TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` (`the readings taken but with F6.1 read as` `the Commissioner must refuse to deregister`) TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` (`the readings taken but with F6.1 read as` `the Law states no rule for that case`) TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- F6.17 A (may deregister any time after the notice): before the objection period ends it may.
#ASSERT `Art 16(1) the time for objections allows deregistration on the day` (`the readings taken but with F6.17 read as` `the Commissioner may deregister at any time after the notice is given`) `ind-b6 a proper notice` (YMD 2026 2 5)
-- F6.17 B (taken) and C on the last day for objections: B no, C yes.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 16(1) the time for objections allows deregistration on the day` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 a proper notice` (YMD 2026 2 10)
#ASSERT `Art 16(1) the time for objections allows deregistration on the day` (`the readings taken but with F6.17 read as` `the Commissioner may deregister only on or after the last day for objections`) `ind-b6 a proper notice` (YMD 2026 2 10)
-- F6.13 B (any time suffices): an unreasonably short time still gives a proper notice.
#ASSERT `Art 16(1) the preliminary notice is the notice the paragraph requires` (`the readings taken but with F6.13 read as` `any time specified suffices`) (`ind-b6 notice` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 16(1) the preliminary notice is the notice the paragraph requires` `ind-b6 A` (`ind-b6 notice` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- F6.2 B (16(2) keeps the 16(1) procedure): no duty without the preliminary notice.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (`Art 16(2) the Commissioner must deregister the entity that no longer exists` (`the readings taken but with F6.2 read as` `Article 16(2) follows the procedure of Article 16(1) and the duty arises only after the prior notice has run its time`) TRUE TRUE NOTHING `ind-b6 day`)
-- F6.19 B (failed whenever the steps are not yet taken).
#ASSERT `Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` (`the readings taken but with F6.19 read as` `the notice has not been complied with whenever the steps have not yet been taken`) (LIST `ind-b6 an unmet notice`) (YMD 2026 1 20)
-- F6.3 B (the notice is the reasons notice) and A-05 reading B: the act of 2020-06-15 is after it, so not protected.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 17(4) the act is not rendered an offence by the retrospective effect` (`the readings taken but with F6.3 read as` `the preliminary notice that gives reasons and invites objections`) `ind-b6 retrospective, notice of 1 July 2020` (YMD 2020 6 15)
-- F6.18 B (29 February rolls to 1 March) and C (the day before the anniversary): the E17-05/E17-06 dates of A-07.
#ASSERT `Art 17(1)(a) the last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` (`the readings taken but with F6.18 read as` `the last day is the anniversary, and 29 February rolls to 1 March`) `ind-b6 deregistered on 29 February 2020` EQUALS YMD 2030 3 1
#ASSERT `Art 17(1)(a) the last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` (`the readings taken but with F6.18 read as` `the last day is the day before the anniversary`) `ind-b6 deregistered on 15 March 2020` EQUALS YMD 2030 3 14
#ASSERT `Art 17(1)(a) the last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` (`the readings taken but with F6.18 read as` `the last day is the day before the anniversary`) `ind-b6 deregistered on 29 February 2020` EQUALS YMD 2030 2 27
-- F6.5 B (the ten years run from the effective date): retrospective to 2020-01-01, the last day is 2030-01-01.
#ASSERT `Art 17(1)(a) the last day on which the Commissioner must retain the information` (`the readings taken but with F6.5 read as` `the ten years run from the date from which the termination takes effect`) `ind-b6 retrospective to 1 January 2020` EQUALS YMD 2030 1 1
-- F6.6 B (the number bar lasts ten years): no bar in 2075.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 17(1)(b) the registered number may not be assigned on the day` (`the readings taken but with F6.6 read as` `the bar on assigning the registered number lasts for the ten years of Article 17(1)(a)`) `ind-b6 deregistered on 15 March 2020` (YMD 2075 1 1)
-- F6.4 B (property acquired before the notice date): retrospective to 2020-01-01, notice 2020-03-15, property acquired 2020-02-01.
#ASSERT `Art 17(5) the property is remaining property` (`the readings taken but with F6.4 read as` `acquired before the date of the deregistration notice`) `ind-b6 retrospective to 1 January 2020` (`ind-b6 property` (YMD 2020 2 1) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 17(5) the property is remaining property` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 retrospective to 1 January 2020` (`ind-b6 property` (YMD 2020 2 1) TRUE)

§ `Positive control for the E17-01 trace (added at review)`

-- With no discard the ten-year prohibition sunsets: waiting past its last day (3652 days after 2020-03-15) gives FULFILLED.
#ASSERT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 17(1)(a) the Commissioner must retain the information for 10 years` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 deregistered on 15 March 2020`) 0 (LIST (`WAIT UNTIL` 3653)))
-- With a discard on day 100, waiting past the last day does not give FULFILLED: the discard was a breach, not a step that leaves the rule standing.
#ASSERT NOT `ind-b6 nothing is owed under` (EVALTRACE (`Art 17(1)(a) the Commissioner must retain the information for 10 years` `ind-b6 A` `ind-b6 deregistered on 15 March 2020`) 0 (LIST EVENT `the Commissioner` (`discard the information registered in respect of the entity` `the Commissioner`) 100, (`WAIT UNTIL` 3653)))
